.nh
.TH "DIFFSCRIBE" "1" "Jan 2026" "diffscribe" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
diffscribe \- LLM-assisted git commit helper

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdiffscribe\fP [\fIprefix\fP] [\fIflags\fP]

.SH DESCRIPTION
diffscribe inspects your staged Git changes and asks an LLM to craft commit
messages that match whatever style you describe via \fB\-\-format\fP (Conventional
Commit summaries by default). Use it directly in the terminal to print
suggestions, or wire it into shell completion so git commit \-m "" followed by
the Tab key yields AI\-generated prefixes that respect whatever you already
typed.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fP=\fIfile\fP
Config file (default searches diffscribe.{yaml,json,toml}).
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fP=\fIdescription\fP
Commit message format description or template. Default: Conventional Commit style (prefix + summary)
.TP
\fB\-\-llm\-api\-key\fP=\fIkey\fP
LLM provider API key.
.TP
\fB\-\-llm\-base\-url\fP=\fIurl\fP
LLM API base URL. Default: https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions
.TP
\fB\-\-llm\-max\-completion\-tokens\fP=\fIn\fP
Max completion tokens to request from the LLM (0 = provider default). Default: 512
.TP
\fB\-\-llm\-model\fP=\fImodel\fP
LLM model identifier. Default: gpt-4o-mini
.TP
\fB\-\-llm\-provider\fP=\fIprovider\fP
LLM provider (openai, openrouter, etc.). Default: openai
.TP
\fB\-\-llm\-temperature\fP=\fIn\fP
LLM sampling temperature. Default: 1
.TP
\fB\-\-quantity\fP=\fIn\fP
Number of suggestions to request. Default: 5
.TP
\fB\-\-system\-prompt\fP=\fIprompt\fP
LLM system prompt override.
.TP
\fB\-\-user\-prompt\fP=\fIprompt\fP
LLM user prompt override.
.TP
\fB\-v\fP, \fB\-\-version\fP
Show version information and exit.
.TP
\fB\-h\fP, \fB\-\-help\fP
Display help and exit.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBDIFFSCRIBE_API_KEY\fP, \fBOPENAI_API_KEY\fP
Provide the LLM provider API key.
.TP
\fBDIFFSCRIBE_STATUS\fP
Set to 0 to hide the "loading..." prompt indicator used by shell integrations.
.TP
\fBDIFFSCRIBE_STASH_COMMIT\fP
Inspect a temporary stash instead of staged changes (used in completions).

.SH FILES
Configuration files are merged in the following order, with later entries
overriding earlier ones for any keys they define:
.TP
\fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/diffscribe/.diffscribe*\fP
User configuration directory (XDG standard).
.TP
\fI$HOME/.diffscribe*\fP
User home directory configuration.
.TP
\fI./.diffscribe*\fP
Project-local configuration.
.PP
Each file only needs to specify the settings it wants to change (for example,
llm.api_key, llm.provider, llm.model, etc.).

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Success.
.TP
1
An error occurred.

.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
# print five suggestions for the staged changes
diffscribe

# constrain results to the provided prefix
diffscribe "feat: add"

# request inline candidates while typing a commit message
git commit -m "feat: "  # then press Tab with the completion scripts installed
.EE

.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgit\fP(1), \fBgit-commit\fP(1)
